Root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect order of operations in the code that handles the finalization of smoke data loading. Specifically, the original code checked if `smoke3di->finalize` was equal to 1 before checking if `return_flag` was set to 1. This could lead to the `SmokeWrapup(smoke3di)` function being called even when the loading process had encountered an error (indicated by `return_flag`), potentially leading to incorrect state management. The patch corrects this by ensuring that `SmokeWrapup(smoke3di)` is only called if `return_flag` is set to 1, thus preventing premature finalization when there are issues with loading the smoke data.
